                    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
                    "body": "Hey! Thanks tons @echasnovski .. it turns out `hop.nvim` was colliding in some way. Not by way of `omap` mappings, but something else I'm wholly unsure of; as soon as I uninstalled it, it worked as expected! I'm not sure when/where that started going awry. No matter though, I switched to using jump2d for hop-like functionality.\r\n\r\nThanks once again!",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">Hey! Thanks tons <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/echasnovski/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski\">@echasnovski</a> .. it turns out <code class=\"notranslate\">hop.nvim</code> was colliding in some way. Not by way of <code class=\"notranslate\">omap</code> mappings, but something else I'm wholly unsure of; as soon as I uninstalled it, it worked as expected! I'm not sure when/where that started going awry. No matter though, I switched to using jump2d for hop-like functionality.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Thanks once again!</p>",
                    "bodyText": "Hey! Thanks tons @echasnovski .. it turns out hop.nvim was colliding in some way. Not by way of omap mappings, but something else I'm wholly unsure of; as soon as I uninstalled it, it worked as expected! I'm not sure when/where that started going awry. No matter though, I switched to using jump2d for hop-like functionality.\nThanks once again!",
