                    "resourcePath": "/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/104#discussioncomment-3322985",
                    "updatedAt": "2022-08-04T07:50:04Z",
                    "upvoteCount": 0,
                    "url": "https://github.com/nvim-mini/mini.nvim/discussions/104#discussioncomment-3322985"
                },
                {
                    "author": {
                        "avatarUrl": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/24854248?u=d09fd974c6720eba3039db6beb2f1c1efecdb51d&v=4",
                        "login": "echasnovski",
                        "resourcePath": "/echasnovski",
                        "url": "https://github.com/echasnovski"
                    },
                    "authorAssociation": "MEMBER",
                    "body": "So I've got to the bottom of this and created an [issue in 'fidget.nvim'](https://github.com/j-hui/fidget.nvim/issues/93). This is not the first time it has encountered this type of issue: it also [happened for 'clever-f'](https://github.com/j-hui/fidget.nvim/issues/68).\r\n\r\nThe reason seems to be quite complex. The 'fidget.nvim' is doing asynchronous update of lines in its window (as it is expected to do). It is wrapped in `vim.schedule()` (how it is supposed to be done). However, if `getchar()` is called inside expression mapping, it blocks Neovim while still trying to execute all asynchronous calls. This results in error, because text can't be changed when Neovim is blocked. This error manifests itself in disabling lua statusline and perform undo on current buffer (no idea why this specifically is done). Honestly, it does seem like an issue on Neovim part.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, both expression mapping and `getchar()` is crucial to 'mini.jump' (and \"user prompt\" textobject from 'mini.ai' in Operator-pending mode, for that matter) as it allows dot-repeat without re-asking for user input.\r\n\r\nFortunately, this seems to be an issue only if 'fidget.nvim' is actively updating its window. Otherwise, they should co-exist without (obvious) problems.\r\n\r\nAll in all, thanks for an interesting case!",
                    "bodyHTML": "<p dir=\"auto\">So I've got to the bottom of this and created an <a href=\"https://github.com/j-hui/fidget.nvim/issues/93\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/j-hui/fidget.nvim/issues/93/hovercard\">issue in 'fidget.nvim'</a>. This is not the first time it has encountered this type of issue: it also <a href=\"https://github.com/j-hui/fidget.nvim/issues/68\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/j-hui/fidget.nvim/issues/68/hovercard\">happened for 'clever-f'</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The reason seems to be quite complex. The 'fidget.nvim' is doing asynchronous update of lines in its window (as it is expected to do). It is wrapped in <code class=\"notranslate\">vim.schedule()</code> (how it is supposed to be done). However, if <code class=\"notranslate\">getchar()</code> is called inside expression mapping, it blocks Neovim while still trying to execute all asynchronous calls. This results in error, because text can't be changed when Neovim is blocked. This error manifests itself in disabling lua statusline and perform undo on current buffer (no idea why this specifically is done). Honestly, it does seem like an issue on Neovim part.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Unfortunately, both expression mapping and <code class=\"notranslate\">getchar()</code> is crucial to 'mini.jump' (and \"user prompt\" textobject from 'mini.ai' in Operator-pending mode, for that matter) as it allows dot-repeat without re-asking for user input.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Fortunately, this seems to be an issue only if 'fidget.nvim' is actively updating its window. Otherwise, they should co-exist without (obvious) problems.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">All in all, thanks for an interesting case!</p>",
                    "bodyText": "So I've got to the bottom of this and created an issue in 'fidget.nvim'. This is not the first time it has encountered this type of issue: it also happened for 'clever-f'.\nThe reason seems to be quite complex. The 'fidget.nvim' is doing asynchronous update of lines in its window (as it is expected to do). It is wrapped in vim.schedule() (how it is supposed to be done). However, if getchar() is called inside expression mapping, it blocks Neovim while still trying to execute all asynchronous calls. This results in error, because text can't be changed when Neovim is blocked. This error manifests itself in disabling lua statusline and perform undo on current buffer (no idea why this specifically is done). Honestly, it does seem like an issue on Neovim part.\nUnfortunately, both expression mapping and getchar() is crucial to 'mini.jump' (and \"user prompt\" textobject from 'mini.ai' in Operator-pending mode, for that matter) as it allows dot-repeat without re-asking for user input.\nFortunately, this seems to be an issue only if 'fidget.nvim' is actively updating its window. Otherwise, they should co-exist without (obvious) problems.\nAll in all, thanks for an interesting case!",
                    "createdAt": "2022-08-04T13:04:05Z",
                    "createdViaEmail": false,
